# lib/ server modules

## Layout

| File | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `validation.ts` | Zod schemas + `z.infer<>` exported types |
| `types.ts` | API response and domain types |
| `constants.ts` | Shared limits and constants |
| `hydradb.ts` | HydraDB client, save, recall |
| `openai.ts` | Grounded answer generation |
| `utils.ts` | `cn()` helper (safe for client import) |

## Env and clients

Read `process.env` only in integration modules (`hydradb.ts`, `openai.ts`). Use factory/getter functions that throw clear errors when env vars are missing.

## Validation

Define limits once in `constants.ts` and reference them in Zod `.max()` calls in `validation.ts`.

## Do not

- Add `"use client"` to any `lib/` file
- Import `hydradb.ts` or `openai.ts` from client components
- Duplicate Zod schemas outside `validation.ts`
